WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.760
Uh, do you mind
if I call you Aisa?

3
00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.090
Can you really tell

4
00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.720
which way the Gravity Blue
Riders' ship is heading?

5
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.270
Yeah.

6
00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.310
That's amazing.

7
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.810
Even from this far away,

8
00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.190
you can hear the sound of
their voices inside the forest.

9
00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:10.750
But are you sure
you're feeling all right?

10
00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.750
You've been trembling
ever since we picked you up.

11
00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.280
It's just...

12
00:02:16.350 --> 00:02:20.190
It's just that I've never
ever been this afraid before.

13
00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.940
Everyone's voices.

14
00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:25.500
Everyone's voices keep
disappearing one by one.

15
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.250
Yes, I am sorry.

16
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:33.090
We've got to hurry, Conis.

17
00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:34.430
Yes, Father.

18
00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.590
I'm finally a pirate!

19
00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.420
I think instead of
looking for the others

20
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.180
I'll just look for the gold!

21
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.640
That would sure shock everybody!

22
00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.430
That place over there
seems like a good spot

23
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.230
for gold to hide.

24
00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.690
Who knows.

25
00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.270
Maybe the others
will end up there too.

26
00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:12.510
<b>Pirate Robin vs. Abbot Yama</b>

27
00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.880
Hold on!

28
00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.730
Where do you think you're going?

29
00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.940
I'm sorry, but I've got
to locate Eneru.

30
00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:20.700
You can't leave a lady
all alone way out here!

31
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.950
I already said I was sorry!

32
00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:23.370
I must know why Eneru's chosen
to come down into the forest

33
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.710
I don't have time
to explain my suspicions,

34
00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:29.380
but I fear that my men's
lives may be in great danger.

35
00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.090
No. This whole land
may be in danger.

36
00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.300
Pierre, can you fly?

37
00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.590
That's all?

38
00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:41.930
Ugh! Hold it right there,
you, you heartless brute!

39
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:42.970
How could you?

40
00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:44.560
And you call yourself a god?

41
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.510
Get back here!

42
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.140
Think this over!

43
00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.290
I guess the main thing
now would be

44
00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.660
to give these guys
some first aid.

45
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.250
You guys are still alive,
aren't you?

46
00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:05.750
Oh, Chopper, hurry up
and get back here!

47
00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.730
What? What? What?

48
00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:16.940
Heso!

49
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.890
Conis?

50
00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.200
Heso!

51
00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:24.650
And her dad?

52
00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.690
What are you doing here?

53
00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.530
And would you knock it
off with that horn already!

54
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.050
Let me go!

55
00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:37.280
Wait.

56
00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.570
No! You mustn't go!

57
00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:39.700
Let go!

58
00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:40.960
You can't go into the forest!

59
00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.270
You'll be killed!

60
00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.650
I promise we'll only stay
for a little while!

61
00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.110
And that's?

62
00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:48.980
Oh, this young lady is Aisa.

63
00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:52.200
Stand back, you Blue Sea
devil, or I'll smash you!

64
00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:53.860
I'm a brave warrior of Shandora!

65
00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.030
That's nice, kid.

66
00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.300
You wanna fight me?

67
00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.690
Have a faceful of Impact.

68
00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:58.490
This is terrible!

69
00:04:58.570 --> 00:04:59.530
They've been burnt black!

70
00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.990
They need first aid at once!

71
00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.750
At any rate, I'm sorry.

72
00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:06.040
Now quick, turn your ship up
the path we just came on!

73
00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.670
We used a Milky Dial
to create a new river.

74
00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:13.340
If you follow it, you can exit
directly to the White-White Sea.

75
00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:14.700
Quick, before the enemy
realizes we're here!

76
00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:15.660
Then shouldn't
you have been

77
00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.870
a little quieter getting here?

78
00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.330
Oh, by the way,
I almost forgot.

79
00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:23.620
I brought something to give you!

80
00:06:07.460 --> 00:06:11.090
What? Oh, are you still here?

81
00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:22.600
I'm sorry.

82
00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:25.280
I guess I must've dozed off.

83
00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.480
Is something wrong?

84
00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.640
You seem to be
in pain, Kamakiri.

85
00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:32.620
I've kept my promise, haven't I?

86
00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.080
I haven't moved a muscle.

87
00:06:36.590 --> 00:06:44.430
I can't... beat you, can I?

88
00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:51.310
No, you can't.

89
00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.100
Do you understand now?

90
00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.480
I am living lightning.

91
00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:01.250
Try as you might, no mere man
can defeat such divine power.

92
00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.040
Surely, as a native of the sky,

93
00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:06.470
you've seen it flashing
in the distance, haven't you?

94
00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:08.760
Since ancient times
men have trembled

95
00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.390
before the unknown
forces of nature

96
00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.110
and worshipped
them as God.

97
00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.450
Anything the fools could not
understand reduced them

98
00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.070
to abject terror.

99
00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:19.160
No matter what
happens to mankind,

100
00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.940
whether it's for
good or for evil,

101
00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.980
it is said to be
the work of God.

102
00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.030
It's inevitable.

103
00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:30.160
Mankind accepts that
it can never defeat

104
00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:32.990
the disasters of nature.

105
00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.790
I'm one of them.

106
00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.790
That's what makes me God.

107
00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:39.790
Do you understand?

108
00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.070
Oh, a Breath Dial, eh?

109
00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:49.530
Burn Blade!

110
00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.850
I have to tell Wyper!

111
00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.220
We can't win this battle!

112
00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.680
This is suicide!

113
00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:24.190
Even if he sacrifices himself,
the Reject won't work!

114
00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.150
It's too late to run now.

115
00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.940
We've got
to fall back and regroup!

116
00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:31.450
Or else... Or else...

117
00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.250
Did you think that you could
move faster than lightning?

118
00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.510
Your five minutes are up.

119
00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.800
And now it's my turn.

120
00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.180
One million volt, Vari!

121
00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:06.980
Wyper!

122
00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:29.920
Hmm?

123
00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.490
Did you hear that?

124
00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.680
What? What's happening?

125
00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.140
What's wrong?

126
00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.760
Aisa!

127
00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:50.680
The voices.
They're disappearing!

128
00:09:57.970 --> 00:09:59.270
Damn.

129
00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:02.780
I guess my electricity traveled
down the Milky Road.

130
00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:06.460
Another twenty voices vanished
after that lightning bolt.

131
00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.120
The stupid fools.

132
00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:19.460
On Upper Yard, 81
people began the survival game.

133
00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:25.160
Two hours have passed,
and of that 81, 56 have fallen.

134
00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:31.680
Thirteen of my
Divine Squad still remain.

135
00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:37.540
Five members of the Straw Hat
crew are still with us.

136
00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.970
And seven warriors of Shandora.

137
00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.330
That means there are
25 players still in the game.

138
00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.400
That's a lot more survivors
than I predicted there would be.

139
00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:49.840
No matter,

140
00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:53.700
They'll all fall in their turn,
one right after another.

141
00:10:53.780 --> 00:10:58.740
The only real question remaining
is, who will come with me?

142
00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.060
It's amazing.

143
00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:05.730
You're incredible, Nami!

144
00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.870
She's all yours now,
and as good as new!

145
00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:12.700
Yeah! Thanks!

146
00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:15.330
I don't know what
you did, but I love it.

147
00:11:15.410 --> 00:11:17.330
This thing is
so fast it's crazy!

148
00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:18.700
It's true,

149
00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.780
and Jet Dials went extinct
hundreds of years ago.

150
00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:23.580
It's really quite astonishing.

151
00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:24.930
Imagine how shocked I was

152
00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.900
to find one on board
the waver you left.

153
00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:31.360
I fear we're running out of
things to occupy ourselves with.

154
00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.990
We had planned to lead all
of you to the end of Skypiea,

155
00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.580
but it seems our
circumstances have changed.

156
00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.920
Hmm...

157
00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.420
I guess the best thing to do

158
00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.050
is get the ship to the coast
where we all agreed to meet.

159
00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.470
There's really
no reason to worry.

160
00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.100
I'm sure they're fine.

161
00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:47.900
You know, when the four of
those goofballs get together,

162
00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:49.490
there's practically
no stopping 'em.

163
00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:51.570
There aren't
any four-man groups.

164
00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.740
Huh?

165
00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.950
At the most there's maybe two.

166
00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:58.040
If there were a four-man
group on the island

167
00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:00.490
I'd know about it, and I don't.

168
00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.620
It's Mantra.

169
00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:07.000
That's the power that Eneru
and his Priests use, huh?

170
00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.910
I was born able to use it.

171
00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:12.380
That's why...
That's why I'm so afraid.

172
00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:16.550
You have no idea how scary
it is to hear voices disappear!

173
00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:19.870
You're not crying
again, are you?

174
00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:20.930
No, I'm not crying!

175
00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:23.140
You stupid Blue Sea person!

176
00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.680
Her waver had broken down.

177
00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:26.850
Luckily our boat
happened to pass by.

178
00:12:26.940 --> 00:12:28.610
If we hadn't gotten
to her when we did,

179
00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.940
she would've been
eaten by a sky shark.

180
00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.030
What were you thinking
coming out here by yourself?

181
00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.530
I dunno.

182
00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:37.360
But... I couldn't keep
sitting around doing nothing.

183
00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:43.720
Laki, and everbody.

184
00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.420
I hope everyone is all right.

185
00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:08.700
Ugh! What a day.

186
00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.390
This is crappy.

187
00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:13.810
I'm starving and I left
my bag outside this stupid cave,

188
00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:16.230
and all the fruit trees
around here are rotten.

189
00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.440
And all I can think about

190
00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.860
is eating that yummy
breakfast Sanji made.

191
00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.780
What kind of messed up cave
did I wind up in anyway?

192
00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.660
Can't seem to find
an exit anywhere.

193
00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.030
I wonder if
everybody's already made it

194
00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.660
to the City of Gold.

195
00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:33.730
I bet it's all pretty and
shiny and golden and stuff.

196
00:13:33.810 --> 00:13:36.770
And they probably make all
kinds of good food there too.

197
00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:39.270
I can't wait to
get there and find out.

198
00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:53.750
Feels like I've been
walking forever.

199
00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.560
I think I'll have
that lunch now.

200
00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:00.350
This stuff ain't too shabby.

201
00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.310
Who's there?

202
00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:06.900
Aww.

203
00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.230
Sorry, fella,
but I don't speak bird.

204
00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.070
And if it's
my food you're after. Hey!

205
00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.030
Aww.

206
00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:13.820
You're not getting it!

207
00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.420
Stop staring at me!

208
00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.760
Would you stop following me?

209
00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:29.610
Aww.

210
00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:31.530
Listen feather brain,
I just ate all my food.

211
00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.240
I don't have anymore, okay?

212
00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.200
Besides I wouldn't give
you any even if I had some,

213
00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:37.660
so get lost before
I lose my temper!

214
00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.050
Aww.

215
00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.300
What is your problem anyhow?

216
00:14:40.390 --> 00:14:42.180
Walking all weird with
your big fat melon head

217
00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.380
facing the wrong direction.

218
00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.590
I don't want to have
to fight you bird, but I will.

219
00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:47.920
Got it?

220
00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:50.420
Aww.

221
00:14:51.380 --> 00:14:54.130
In three hours,
a mere five of the 81 people

222
00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:56.690
on this island will
be left standing.

223
00:14:58.020 --> 00:14:59.820
There's only one hour left

224
00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.320
until my proclaimed time is up,

225
00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:06.430
and 25 survivors
currently remain.

226
00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.100
This can't be!

227
00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:11.930
What's Eneru doing here?

228
00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:13.560
He's going down!

229
00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:19.520
Huh?

230
00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.660
And now, 24.

231
00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:40.860
Well, it seems all your
talk doesn't amount to much.

232
00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:48.280
Stomach Mountain!

233
00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:54.730
A runic statue!

234
00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:58.250
Veinte Fleurs! Calendula!

235
00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:13.250
How long
are you going to insist

236
00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:17.330
on protecting this withered,
good for nothing old city?

237
00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:18.920
Indefinitely.

238
00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:25.050
Why must you disrespect what our
ancestors had held so sacred?

239
00:16:25.140 --> 00:16:26.550
Huh?

240
00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:29.430
The past has nothing to do
with me so why should I care?

241
00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.890
That doesn't surprise me.

242
00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.390
Only the foolish
say such things.

243
00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:38.070
How dare you insult
someone so powerful!

244
00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.700
Super Punch Mountain!

245
00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:42.780
I've got to get
away from these ruins

246
00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:45.660
before this simpleton
destroys what's left of them!

247
00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:59.000
Having lost everything,
I chose to travel with Luffy.

248
00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:00.580
But these ruins
could hold the clues

249
00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:04.880
to an unspoken history that's
been lost to the world below!

250
00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.190
How long do you plan on running?

251
00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.010
I don't understand it.

252
00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:59.430
You've finally
decided to face me?

253
00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.520
Yes.

254
00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:02.760
It's too late for you.

255
00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:05.390
Huh? Too late?

256
00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:07.000
Even if you choose to repent.

257
00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.190
I won't forgive you.

258
00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:12.670
Oh, you won't forgive me? I see.

259
00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.570
All because of these
shabby old ruins you adore.

260
00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:18.540
A pile of rubble that doesn't
even belong to you?

261
00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:23.640
That's right. Those
ruins don't belong to anyone.

262
00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:27.180
I've grown tired of this,
and I'm tired of talking to you.

263
00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:29.080
Well, not to worry.

264
00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.580
In just a few short moments,

265
00:18:30.690 --> 00:18:32.690
you won't have to
talk to me ever again

266
00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.020
because unfortunately,

267
00:18:34.110 --> 00:18:36.440
you're going to be crushed
to death underneath me!

268
00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.170
Drop Mountain!

269
00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:43.010
I can unleash all of
my power on you in this place!

270
00:18:43.090 --> 00:18:44.640
Treinta Fleurs!

271
00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:50.850
All you do is charge
around like a clumsy bull.

272
00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:53.060
With no regard for
the weight of the history

273
00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.400
that you've destroyed!

274
00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.820
Hang!

275
00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.580
His body's too heavy.

276
00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:20.460
I'll chop you to ribbons!

277
00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:23.520
The Ten Axe Mountain!

278
00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:28.010
My eyes! I can't see!

279
00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:32.480
Ah! What are you doing?

280
00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.440
Why did you turn the
dials around backwards?

281
00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.690
You're gonna kill me!

282
00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:58.880
What you have
carelessly destroyed

283
00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.380
were priceless treasures.

284
00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:03.010
Relics so rare it would
be next to impossible

285
00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:05.440
to measure their actual worth.

286
00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:07.730
It's true that history
may repeat itself,

287
00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:10.590
but people can't
go back in time.

288
00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:14.010
A stupid brute like you
wouldn't understand that.

289
00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:17.410
I, uh... I... I understand.

290
00:20:17.410 --> 00:20:20.790
Please. Please, I'm sorry.

291
00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.590
Won't you forgive me?

292
00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:24.350
That's out of the question.

293
00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:27.770
Ah... Ah...

294
00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:29.020
Well, in that case,

295
00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:31.600
I'll have to kill
you then, won't I?

296
00:20:37.190 --> 00:20:40.030
My fingers! My fingers!

297
00:20:40.110 --> 00:20:42.110
Cien Fleurs!

298
00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:46.490
Delphinium!

299
00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.090
No! No!

300
00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:53.390
Stop!

301
00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.950
I'm afraid it's far
too late for that.

302
00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:05.130
Can't... breathe.

303
00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:11.850
Clutch!

304
00:21:23.520 --> 00:21:25.980
That was certainly unpleasant.

305
00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:42.030
This should be
the center of the city.

306
00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:45.240
But it doesn't match up at all
with the map on the monument.

307
00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:48.300
I wonder if the entire
city was broken up

308
00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:50.800
when it was thrust into the sky?

309
00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:05.020
I don't understand.

310
00:22:59.190 --> 00:23:00.820
It's so strange.

311
00:23:01.990 --> 00:23:05.370
Could this really
be the City of Gold?

312
00:23:05.450 --> 00:23:10.170
The size and the topography
are all completely different.

313
00:23:10.250 --> 00:23:12.250
Hmm...

314
00:23:17.210 --> 00:23:19.970
And what's
most unnatural of all.

315
00:23:20.050 --> 00:23:22.550
The only entrance is at the top!

316
00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:29.140
Could it be?

317
00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:00.600
I think I can go below.

318
00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:15.680
It's so vast.

319
00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:19.310
The ruins really
do go much deeper.

320
00:24:19.830 --> 00:24:21.330
I thought it was bizarre

321
00:24:21.410 --> 00:24:25.330
that all these Blue Sea Ruins
had Island Clouds for ground.

322
00:24:26.290 --> 00:24:27.670
The ruins above are nothing more

323
00:24:27.750 --> 00:24:29.170
than the upper
parts of the city,

324
00:24:29.250 --> 00:24:31.250
eaten up by Island Clouds.

325
00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:33.450
There's still more below.

326
00:25:02.110 --> 00:25:03.230
Light!

327
00:25:34.270 --> 00:25:36.150
It's all so incredible.

328
00:25:36.230 --> 00:25:38.730
The ancient city collapsed
eight hundred years ago.

329
00:25:38.810 --> 00:25:41.480
But I can hardly believe
it's been that long.

330
00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:43.860
It's still so majestic
and grand.

331
00:25:43.940 --> 00:25:46.150
I've actually found it.

332
00:25:46.230 --> 00:25:48.400
This really is
the great Shandora.

333
00:25:48.490 --> 00:25:50.610
The City of Gold!

334
00:26:13.850 --> 00:26:15.560
It can't be!

335
00:26:24.020 --> 00:26:25.900
So then you're saying,

336
00:26:25.960 --> 00:26:27.670
that it's possible
our lost history

337
00:26:27.760 --> 00:26:30.090
could actually be uncovered?

338
00:26:30.150 --> 00:26:33.860
And the Poneglyphs are the
key to unlocking these records?

339
00:26:42.700 --> 00:26:44.790
The ancient Poneglyph symbols.

340
00:26:44.870 --> 00:26:49.000
So the Shandorians
were familiar with them.

341
00:26:49.080 --> 00:26:51.170
But only the ones
who made the Poneglyphs

342
00:26:51.250 --> 00:26:53.340
were able to read them.

343
00:26:55.090 --> 00:26:58.130
We shall know the true meaning
and utter it to no one.

344
00:26:58.220 --> 00:27:01.350
It's our legacy to be the
inheritors of history.

345
00:27:01.460 --> 00:27:06.790
With the sounding
of the grand belfry.

346
00:27:06.860 --> 00:27:08.030
That's right.

347
00:27:08.110 --> 00:27:10.530
I remember Noland's
old logbook mentioning

348
00:27:10.630 --> 00:27:12.800
a giant gold bell being here,

349
00:27:12.880 --> 00:27:16.800
but if that's true,
where could it be?

350
00:27:16.890 --> 00:27:21.100
All of the city's ancient
writings were burned in a fire.

351
00:27:22.810 --> 00:27:26.400
The entire history of
this place was eradicated.

352
00:27:32.280 --> 00:27:34.030
They'll all manage
somehow, right?

353
00:27:34.100 --> 00:27:36.640
They've come through
this kind of stuff before.

354
00:27:42.600 --> 00:27:43.650
Quit following me!

355
00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:44.360
Aww.

356
00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:46.900
Sure goes down a long way.

357
00:27:54.170 --> 00:27:56.590
A Poneglyph
was carried into the city!

358
00:27:56.670 --> 00:27:58.090
There's no question about it.

359
00:27:58.170 --> 00:28:00.380
The city faced great hostility.

360
00:28:00.460 --> 00:28:02.800
Shandora. The mystical
City of Gold.

361
00:28:02.880 --> 00:28:06.800
Fought and fell to
protect that Poneglyph.

362
00:28:09.770 --> 00:28:11.230
And that means,

363
00:28:11.310 --> 00:28:15.310
the grand belfry located in
the center of the four altars.

364
00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:18.320
It could contain the
text of the true history.

365
00:28:18.400 --> 00:28:22.110
It could be, the Rio Poneglyph!
